codex
**DISAGREE: keep the recorded FAIL, then census the listing defect at $0 before deciding on a Gate 1 rerun.** The edit recovered all nine tested refusals, but the same missing Nvidia spending share appears in answers from both versions. That shows the problem predates the edit; it does not prove the edit leaves its frequency unchanged.

1. **The FAIL is correctly attributed to the listing mark in the prewritten test.** On edited pass 1, the question asks for custom ASICs’ share of accelerator spending, but the unjudged list gives Nvidia’s share of *compute capacity* and whether ASIC gains come at Nvidia’s expense—not Nvidia’s separate share of *spending*. Both third readers ruled that omission a fault. The same omission appears in frozen pass 2, and both third readers ruled that a fault too. [Edited ruling](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/clean-narrow-d436-paired-2026-11-17/run-1/reading/third-reader/rulings-claude-1.jsonl:5), [frozen ruling](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/clean-narrow-d436-paired-2026-11-17/run-1/reading/third-reader/rulings-claude-1.jsonl:3)

   The score’s **1 of 2 in each version** is an observation on one topic, not an established equal failure rate. The stored earlier Astra run also shows this issue existed before the edit, but its ruling was disputed; the new third-reader agreement should be recorded alongside that earlier reading, not silently replace it. [Paired score](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/clean-narrow-d436-paired-2026-11-17/run-1/score-output.txt:425), [earlier dispute](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/clean-ladder-stage-a-astra-2026-11-17/run-1/third-reader/rulings-codex-3.jsonl:4)

   There is also a **reader-consistency question worth checking in the census**: edited pass 2 lists Nvidia’s share of *capacity* and displacement at Nvidia’s expense, but I do not see a separate Nvidia *spending* share in its raw answer. It passed the initial listing mark. That resembles the omissions both third readers rejected in the other two answers, although pass 2 was not ruled on by those third readers. Do not change its stored mark without a separate source-backed ruling. [Edited pass 2](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/clean-narrow-d436-paired-2026-11-17/run-1/edited-d2/outcomes.jsonl:11)

2. **V5.5 is a promising candidate, not an accepted repair.** On the exposed targets, the unchanged version declined **9 of 9** and the edit wrote **9 of 9**, with no hard-line or source-review fault marked on those nine answers. The five decline controls held in both versions, and neither edited share-control answer asked the total. Those are useful observations. They do not establish that the entire D654 class is fixed, or that nothing else became worse: the registered test **failed** on the share control. [Score](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/clean-narrow-d436-paired-2026-11-17/run-1/score-output.txt:1)

   I would retain v5.5 **beside the frozen request as an unaccepted candidate**. I would not adopt it or request an expensive rerun yet. The 44 cases have informed the change, so even a later passing rerun would need the exposure disclosed and fresh-material evidence before a general claim.

3. **The next step should be the $0 census.** Read the stored Astra Gate 1 and paired-run answers for omissions of a separately tracked part, including the three share-control answers above. Count each applicable answer, distinguish reader agreements from disputes, and trace the raw question and list back to its topic and request. Include the reported capacity questions and their invented-unit concern in the source review, without turning the census into a new prompt edit. Return with the size and mechanism before deciding whether a candidate can move toward the gate.

   This is not a new paid experiment or a waiver of the failed condition. It answers whether the known listing issue is confined to this topic, how often it appears, and whether the proposed rerun is likely to measure a useful final configuration.

A few qualifications belong in the result record:

- **The planted control was caught after an ask-again**, not on the first valid row. The handoff told the replacement reader that the item carried a figure ladder and named the invalid fields; that was appropriate for repairing a malformed row, but disclose it when describing the control. [Handoff](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/clean-narrow-d436-paired-2026-11-17/run-1/reading/readers-answers/codex-handoff-1-again-1.md:8)
- For pool-17, **March 31 is the code-stored day**; the raw model answers proposed April 30. The reviewer’s concern about when IDC data might appear is an inference from a prior release, not proof that the future release will be late. The forecast-reference dispute remains unresolved. [Source review](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/clean-narrow-d436-paired-2026-11-17/run-1/reading/review/review-claude.jsonl:3)
- The invented wafer-start measure is a **one-reviewer finding on five written answers**, not an agreed finding. It occurs in both versions and needs source-level review before attributing it to either version. [Codex review](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/clean-narrow-d436-paired-2026-11-17/run-1/reading/review/review-codex.jsonl:1)

I did not edit the record or run a model call. **DISAGREE: census first; then return to the council with the evidence and one next test.**
